KNOWNBUG: [temp.variadic] / [class.base.init] -- forwarding a function parameter
pack to a base-class initializer that has a non-pack argument before the pack
expansion (`Base(tag, args...)`) does not propagate the pack: the base subobject
is left default-constructed.  A member initializer of the same shape works; only
the base-class case is affected.  This is std::optional's construction shape
(`_Optional_base(in_place, forward<Args>(args)...)`), and is why
`std::optional<int> o = 5; o.value()` fails (the optional ends up disengaged).
Flip to CORE once fixed.
